---
import Simple from '../../layouts/Simple.astro';
---
<Simple title="Google vs Microsoft 365 vs Azure for Cold Email"
  description="Which sending platform to buy, decided by your recipient mix and your tolerance for concentrated failure."
  eyebrow="Compare" h1="Google, Microsoft 365 or Azure"
  lede="Three genuinely different products. The right answer follows from your recipient mix, not from preference.">
  <div class="scroll-x" style="margin:28px 0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Google Workspace</th><th>Microsoft 365</th><th>Azure tenant</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Gmail-heavy lists</td><td>Outlook-heavy lists</td><td>Volume at low cost</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sold as</td><td>Packs of 3</td><td>Packs of 3</td><td>100 per tenant</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Per inbox cost</td><td>Higher</td><td>Higher</td><td class="yes">Far lower</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Failure blast radius</td><td class="yes">One domain</td><td class="yes">One domain</td><td class="no">The tenant</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Diagnostics when filtered</td><td class="no">Minimal</td><td class="yes">Headers state the reason</td><td class="yes">Headers state the reason</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Admin surface</td><td>Google Admin</td><td>Exchange admin</td><td>Entra admin centre</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2>Decide on the mix, not the brand</h2>
  <p>Segment your list by receiving provider before you buy anything. A file that is two thirds Google and a file that is two thirds Microsoft want different infrastructure, and the segmentation takes minutes.</p>
  <h2>Where the Azure trade sits</h2>
  <p>A tenant is not simply cheaper inboxes. It buys a safer volume shape, because 1,500 sends across 100 mailboxes is 15 each rather than 150 each. It also concentrates reputation into one pool, so an unverified list can affect all hundred at once. Under roughly 1,000 sends a day the isolation of packs is usually worth more than the saving.</p>
  <p><a href="/prewarmed-azure-inboxes/">The Azure risk model in full →</a></p>
</Simple>
